#: ../../source/architecture.rst:2 4548ffc0f314442f8d397619592dc65b
msgid "_`Architecture`"
msgstr ""
"_`架构`"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:4 a11679c091234558b0062276d19571b0
msgid ""
"This page answers the question the reference documentation does not: "
"**why is the library shaped this way**. It is written for three readers "
"-- the architect deciding whether this belongs in a product, the reviewer"
" deciding whether its shape holds, and the integrator deciding where they"
" are expected to cut."
msgstr ""
"本页回答参考文档不去回答的那个问题： **这个库为什么长成这个样子** 。它面"
"向三类读者——判断它是否该进产品的架构师，判断它的形状是否站得住的评审者，"
"以及判断自己该在哪里切开的集成者。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:10 df5d2c02bf9d4628ad149c688f01dde7
msgid "The position"
msgstr ""
"立场"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:12 a00f288027864b6c8116d29cb5a1a17d
msgid ""
"Most motor-control software is one of four things, and each is right for "
"somebody. A vendor SDK brings a working drive on one part family and the "
"vendor's abstraction with it. A model-based toolchain generates code from"
" a block diagram. A research library lives where iteration is cheap. A "
"framework owns the application, including the loop and the memory."
msgstr ""
"多数电机控制软件是四类东西之一，每一类都对某类人合适。厂商 SDK 带来在某"
"个芯片系列上能跑的驱动器，也把厂商的抽象一并带来。基于模型的工具链从框图"
"生成代码。研究型库栖身在迭代便宜的地方。框架占有应用，包括环和内存。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:17 836fbe7718b548339ca821eb94e5ba6d
msgid ""
"The position this library takes is the space those leave: **a core that "
"can be handed to a reviewer, whose cost is bounded by construction, whose"
" numerical behaviour is argued rather than asserted, and which is the "
"same code from C++, from C and from a script.**"
msgstr ""
"本库取的是这四类留出来的空档： **一个能交到评审者手里的内核——代价由构造"
"方式界定，数值行为是被论证的而不是被断言的，并且从 C++、从 C、从脚本看都"
"是同一份代码。**"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:21 0354ab908deb4db29fb6971f16a1785e
msgid ""
"That position is a set of refusals, and each is a decision rather than a "
"preference:"
msgstr ""
"这个立场是一组拒绝，每一条都是决定，而不是偏好："

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:23 dc419813fbfe4697b45c7587e312dabb
msgid ""
"**no heap in the loop**, which forbids containers and buys a worst case "
"that can be written down;"
msgstr ""
"**环里没有堆** ，因此禁用容器，换来一个可以写在纸上的最坏情形；"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:25 aaca7a82132c466cbbd032862d781225
msgid ""
"**no exceptions and no RTTI**, which buys an error path whose cost is a "
"returned value;"
msgstr ""
"**不用异常，也不用 RTTI** ，换来一条代价只是一个返回值的错误路径；"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:26 08e43a9ae14144308fdb376b08a056de
msgid ""
"**no virtual dispatch on the periodic path**, which buys inlining through"
" the whole chain;"
msgstr ""
"**周期路径上没有虚分派** ，换来整条链路的内联；"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:27 e8611d33b91b4a42bbbe17da558fa275
msgid ""
"**no defaults that could hide a fault**, which buys a boot that fails "
"loudly instead of a protection that was never enabled."
msgstr ""
"**不留可能掩盖故障的默认值** ，换来一次会大声失败的上电，而不是一条从未"
"被使能的保护。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:31 cc074d1269304caf869de5d17fcad9e6
msgid "What a breadth-first library optimises for, and what changes here"
msgstr ""
"广度优先的库优化什么，这里改了什么"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:33 67730c88583749a1bd17d29c5ce12d2c
msgid ""
"The architecture chapter of a large library is a map of a breadth-first "
"system: the module graph, the data objects that flow through it, how to "
"plug in a new algorithm, which backends are interchangeable. Those "
"libraries are judged on coverage and on being a substrate for other "
"people's work, so they are optimised for **extension volume**."
msgstr ""
"大型库的架构章节画的是广度优先系统的地图：模块图、在其中流动的数据对象、"
"如何插入新算法、哪些后端可互换。这类库按覆盖面和能否当他人的工作底座来评"
"判，因此优化的是 **扩展体量** 。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:38 607dbad4bca34d918cf4c78077af553f
msgid ""
"A hard-real-time core is optimised for the opposite: a small number of "
"seams, each of them compile-time, and a cost that does not depend on the "
"input. The dimensions are the same and the answers are inverted."
msgstr ""
"硬实时内核优化的方向正相反：接缝数量少，每条都在编译期，代价与输入无关。"
"维度相同，答案相反。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:42 1ca6c53519b64655afb267f149865a45
msgid "The same dimensions, the opposite answers"
msgstr ""
"同样的维度，相反的答案"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:46 5a6563d13d4740968668278558cc0e68
msgid "Dimension"
msgstr ""
"维度"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:47 fa634849145f4751b6e76c1459b6af0d
msgid "A breadth-first library"
msgstr ""
"广度优先的库"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:48 dae057d107a04612be39857ffaeea70a
msgid "This one, and why"
msgstr ""
"本库，以及理由"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:49 e09d3f543c83410eb915c50da9bab8ea
msgid "Extensibility"
msgstr ""
"可扩展性"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:50 2359e34ed56341e981da5ec61c8015b4
msgid "hundreds of algorithms behind one interface, discovered at run time"
msgstr ""
"成百上千种算法藏在一个接口背后，运行期才发现"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:51 38ebb54568c54e1e9acf4c7e56b5f2a6
msgid ""
"four policy seams, fixed at compile time, because a run-time lookup is a "
"cost the loop cannot audit"
msgstr ""
"四条策略接缝，编译期固定，因为一次运行期查找是环无法审计的代价"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:53 b71f5a09c7a548e284c9c371df53f4f7
msgid "Object model"
msgstr ""
"对象模型"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:54 fe09d029e4ad45e0b878872d63fea1a8
msgid "deep hierarchies, shared ownership, reference counting"
msgstr ""
"深层继承、共享所有权、引用计数"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:55 7372d311f32c4b08802986de8ab33859
msgid ""
"value types and composition; ownership stays with the caller, so there is"
" nothing to count and nothing to leak"
msgstr ""
"值类型与组合；所有权留在调用方，因此没有东西要计数，也没有东西会泄漏"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:57 df9c526b07d645eb99c7b53daad1bd79
msgid "Data flow"
msgstr ""
"数据流"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:58 e0ae3f0fd09b461b925ee66f4e162317
msgid "images and meshes through a pipeline of stages"
msgstr ""
"图像与网格穿过一条分级流水线"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:59 f3f078a111aa4104a789e468ef2df5e6
msgid ""
"one request and three duties per period; the state is the controller's, "
"not the library's"
msgstr ""
"每个周期一次请求、三项职责；状态属于控制器，不属于库"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:61 49b46be9995f49e790e520e323dd548d
msgid "Backends"
msgstr ""
"后端"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:62 71d01e88b5544ffaa5774ef8326c43ce
msgid "interchangeable, selected by configuration"
msgstr ""
"可互换，由配置选择"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:63 8437d218722a4a7996e11e36fee16bfe
msgid "one HAL policy per build; the hardware is not a run-time detail"
msgstr ""
"每次构建一个 HAL 策略；硬件不是运行期细节"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:64 afb3b7b6f79147299e27287233f987c0
msgid "Error model"
msgstr ""
"错误模型"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:65 136d0257f44e4b5fb80e8d457abbaea7
msgid "exceptions or status trees, because failure is rare and deferred"
msgstr ""
"异常或状态树，因为失败罕见且被推迟处理"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:66 2e2724776beb4281838e4cea27bd5980
msgid ""
"a closed set of returned codes, because failure must be decided in the "
"same period"
msgstr ""
"一组封闭的返回码，因为失败必须在同一个周期内定下来"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:67 ea8183f41e2a4af1871114d52b590e51
msgid "Binary compatibility"
msgstr ""
"二进制兼容"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:68 56e3c1ad6e954fe6a0ab660c841fc87e
msgid "versioned libraries, plugins, symbol visibility"
msgstr ""
"带版本的库、插件、符号可见性"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:69 e398beb4f1ca4a8d985e82656414d043
msgid "a frozen C surface with size-tagged structs and generation-checked handles"
msgstr ""
"冻结的 C 使用面，结构体自带长度标记，句柄带代数校验"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:70 2c3920383dfe419ead73014e98eea672
msgid "Cost model"
msgstr ""
"代价模型"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:71 26589426232b4f66a458f4c0c689eda3
msgid "measured per operation, optimised per backend"
msgstr ""
"逐操作测量，逐后端优化"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:72 8a853daaa60c46f09439e46ff52f8c70
msgid "bounded by construction: no allocation, no dispatch, no exception"
msgstr ""
"由构造方式本身界定：不分配、不分派、不抛异常"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:74 a9dae710521b4635a4e7d92b0da93426
msgid ""
"Two consequences surprise readers arriving from a breadth-first library. "
"There is **no plugin architecture**, and that is not an omission: adding "
"an observer is a template argument plus a case, and the compiler is the "
"registration mechanism. And the **C surface exists for the opposite "
"reason a C API usually exists** -- not to let other languages in, but to "
"give the core a boundary that cannot grow accidentally, since every "
"declaration there is a promise about the next decade."
msgstr ""
"对从广度优先库过来的人，有两处结论出乎意料。其一， **没有插件架构** ，这"
"不是遗漏：增加一个观测器就是一个模板实参加一个 case 分支，编译器就是注册"
"机制。其二， **C 使用面存在的理由，与通常的 C API 相反** ——不是为了让别"
"的语言进来，而是给内核一条不会意外生长的边界，因为那里的每一条声明都是关"
"于未来十年的承诺。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:82 a392a460543a49d28f7b107b8ce55900
msgid "Three faces, one core"
msgstr ""
"三个使用面，一个内核"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:84 45ea0d2a12ba469cb88139dfa245f115
msgid ""
"The core cannot be written in the language of any one consumer: it is "
"value types and functions over them, and each face is a thin adaptation."
msgstr ""
"内核不能用任何一个使用方的语言来写：它是值类型，以及作用于这些值类型的函"
"数；每个使用面都只是一层薄适配。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:92 615f90600b864eae9e8c97623a9c2033
msgid ""
"Each arrow points inward. No face knows about another, and Python reaches"
" the core only through the C surface."
msgstr ""
"每条箭头都指向内部。使用面彼此不相识，Python 只能经由 C 使用面触到内核。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:95 5b834904f8d64445a70958bf854b5779
msgid ""
"The dependency direction is not a style preference. If Python could reach"
" the templates directly, the C surface would stop being a constraint on "
"it and the two surfaces would drift, with the tests of one silently not "
"covering the other."
msgstr ""
"依赖方向不是风格偏好。如果 Python 能直接够到模板，C 使用面就不再是对它的"
"约束，两个使用面会各自漂移，一边的用例悄悄盖不住另一边。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:100 711d1069044b4bad9c0db98322380a4a
msgid "The loop, composed rather than inherited"
msgstr ""
"环由组合而来，不是继承而来"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:102 71abd1f47e4d4575a8a847ec46378f8f
msgid ""
"The periodic path is a composition of policies fixed at compile time: the"
" HAL is a template parameter, the modulator is a template parameter, the "
"regulator is a template parameter, and the composition is a type."
msgstr ""
"周期路径是若干编译期固定的策略的组合：HAL 是模板实参，调制器是模板实参，"
"调节器是模板实参，而组合本身是一个类型。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:111 e1b18f477d2c40cc9ba32052a1a83e38
msgid ""
"One PWM period: the reference, the regulators, the limits, the modulator,"
" the minimum-pulse stage, the HAL, and the observer closing the loop "
"through the angle."
msgstr ""
"一个 PWM 周期：给定、调节器、限幅、调制器、最小脉宽级、HAL，以及经由角度"
"把环闭合的观测器。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:114 c67e9e1f339542cfbbab8e6ff7ac0722
msgid ""
"Two asymmetries in that picture are where this differs from a textbook "
"cascade. The **limits are inside the chain** rather than at its output, "
"so a regulator knows the ceiling it is working against rather than "
"discovering it afterwards. And the **minimum-pulse and dead-time stage "
"sits between the modulator and the HAL**, because those losses happen "
"between arithmetic and copper and nothing downstream can infer them."
msgstr ""
"图里有两处不对称，正是本库与教科书式级联的分野。其一， **限幅在链路内部*"
"* ，而不在链路出口，因此调节器事先就知道自己顶着哪个上限，不必事后才发现"
"。其二， **最小脉宽与死区这一级夹在调制器与 HAL 之间** ，因为这些损失发"
"生在算术与铜线之间，下游任何环节都推断不出来。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:121 9acdbdf4fa52430bab8b5a09c4f2c7c9
msgid "The layering, and what may depend on what"
msgstr ""
"分层，以及谁可以依赖谁"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:128 dc01f03a156048a885f0d45414838382
msgid ""
"Header layers. The value layer is the floor: everything may depend on it "
"and it depends on nothing but the standard library. The HAL appears as a "
"box with no arrows out, because it is a policy the caller implements "
"rather than a module the library calls."
msgstr ""
"头文件分层。值层是地板：任何东西都可以依赖它，而它除标准库之外不依赖任何"
"东西。HAL 画成一个没有出箭头的方框，因为它是调用方实现的策略，而不是库去"
"调用的模块。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:132 6b0bffc2cf37465fbb5e1b905800a1f7
msgid ""
"Two rules hold the picture up. **A third-party header may not reach a "
"public header**: the cost was measured to be multiples of the entire "
"include face, so the answer is no rather than \"only a little\", and the "
"dependency gate is what says so. And **the C face is a mirror, not a "
"dependency**: ``foc_types.h`` is written by hand against the value "
"layer's semantics rather than generated from it, because a generated "
"mirror breaks whenever the generator does -- and it breaks in the ABI."
msgstr ""
"两条规则撑起这张图。其一， **第三方头文件不得进入公开头文件** ：代价实测"
"是整个 include 面的数倍，所以答案是“不行”，而不是“只一点点”，这么回答的"
"是依赖门禁。其二， **C 使用面是镜像，不是依赖** ： ``foc_types.h`` 是照"
"着值层的语义手写的，而不是从值层生成的，因为生成的镜像会随生成器一起坏——"
"而且坏在 ABI 上。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:140 9e72b2bd70b54ab69079f2ce2e45d0a0
msgid "The data model"
msgstr ""
"数据模型"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:142 1948e62ff28f47c4b303e15a1aa5eab2
msgid ""
"Everything that flows through the library is a small value type whose "
"name says what it is: a phase triple, a stationary pair, a rotor-frame "
"pair, a configuration struct, a result struct. They are trivially "
"copyable, they have no invariants a constructor must defend, and the "
"library never owns them."
msgstr ""
"在库里流动的一切都是小的值类型，名字即其所是：三相三元组、静止坐标系下的"
"一对、转子坐标系下的一对、配置结构体、结果结构体。它们可平凡复制，没有需"
"要构造函数去守住的不变量，库也从不持有它们。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:147 eed83242f7bc4d62b1a07d2cb31a4da9
msgid ""
"Three properties follow. **No aliasing**: a function that takes a value "
"cannot be affected by another context mutating it, so \"who else holds "
"this\" never arises in the loop. **No hidden state**: a result struct "
"carries what the caller needs to decide what happened -- a saturation "
"flag, a mask, a timestamp and a status -- so nobody has to ask the object"
" what it meant. **Units in the names**: the symbol registry generates the"
" symbol table, and a quantity without a registered unit fails the "
"documentation's gates, which is a cheap way to make \"milliseconds where "
"seconds were expected\" a visible mistake."
msgstr ""
"由此有三条性质。其一， **没有别名** ：按值取参的函数，不会被另一处上下文"
"改写它而影响，因此“还有谁持有它”在环里从不成为问题。其二， **没有隐藏状"
"态** ：结果结构体带着调用方判断发生了什么所需的一切——饱和标志、掩码、时"
"间戳与状态，没有人需要再去问那个对象它是什么意思。其三， **单位写在名字"
"里** ：符号注册表生成符号表，一个没有登记单位的量过不了文档门禁，这是让“"
"该用秒的地方写成毫秒”变成可见错误的便宜办法。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:156 5038cf2d5ad74161b17df3fc0da40916
msgid "The failure model"
msgstr ""
"失败模型"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:158 9fac4d58bce34f03a802187045462bd5
msgid "Failure is a value with a small closed set of meanings."
msgstr ""
"失败是一个值，含义是一个小的封闭集合。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:165 a6e9c82a33aa4c6eb0ef995dc5a3632f
msgid ""
"What can go wrong and which code carries it. The distinction that matters"
" operationally is between \"you asked wrong\" and \"this build cannot\"."
msgstr ""
"会出什么错，由哪个码承载。运行中真正要紧的区分，是“你问错了”和“这次构建"
"做不到”之间的区分。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:168 84102eed38e54f43a786501dad7a59af
msgid ""
"That distinction is not pedantry. Some fields of the host setup structure"
" are appended over time, and an absent one means the caller was compiled "
"against an older header rather than that the value is zero. A call that "
"needs an absent field answers *not implemented*, because otherwise \"we "
"never asked\" reads like \"nothing is wrong\" -- and the caller's "
"recovery differs: one is fixed by passing the value, the other by "
"rebuilding."
msgstr ""
"这条区分不是咬文嚼字。主机设置结构体的某些字段是随时间追加的，字段缺席意"
"味着调用方是按更旧的头文件编译的，而不是那个值是零。需要某个缺席字段的调"
"用会回答 *未实现* ，否则“从没问过”读起来就像“没有问题”——而调用方的补救方"
"式不同：一种靠把值传进去，另一种靠重新构建。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:174 3a2d7f8fd04d4a38a6e58542017ab37e
msgid ""
"Two conventions complete the model. **Refusals happen before work**: a "
"configuration that cannot be run is rejected at construction or at the "
"first call that needs it. And **diagnostics saturate rather than wrap**: "
"a loss counter that wraps to zero reports \"nothing lost\" at the moment "
"everything was lost."
msgstr ""
"两条约定补全这个模型。其一， **拒绝发生在干活之前** ：跑不起来的配置在构"
"造时就被拒掉，或者在第一次需要它时被拒掉。其二， **诊断量饱和而不回绕** "
"：一个回绕到零的丢失计数器，会在一切都丢了的那一刻报告“没有丢失”。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:180 789d2c1176ca480f898604f41dbdabd1
msgid "The configuration model"
msgstr ""
"配置模型"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:182 e884120a7cfd47cd897601bdeb2a2569
msgid ""
"Configuration is a struct passed at construction, readable but never "
"partly written. That is stronger than it looks: there is no moment at "
"which a running drive has a mixture of old and new settings, which is the"
" failure mode of a setter-based interface in a system with a periodic "
"interrupt."
msgstr ""
"配置是一个在构造时传入的结构体，可读，但从不被部分写入。这比看上去更硬："
"不存在某一刻运行中的驱动器混着新旧两套设置，而这正是带周期中断的系统里、"
"基于 setter 的接口的失效方式。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:187 569f778fa851413a908e335bd5d5398a
msgid ""
"Values divide into two kinds, and the division is visible in the types. "
"**Boot-time** values -- pole pairs, dead time, switching period, current "
"limits -- describe the hardware and are fixed for the life of the object."
" **Run-time** values -- references, enables, mode -- are commands and are"
" functions rather than fields. Mixing the two is the most common silent "
"integration error after a wrong pole count, because a dead time copied "
"onto a different bridge behaves exactly like a machine whose resistance "
"is wrong."
msgstr ""
"取值分两类，分野在类型上看得见。 **上电期** 取值——极对数、死区、开关周期"
"、电流限值——描述硬件，在对象的整个生命期内固定。 **运行期** 取值——给定、"
"使能、模式——是命令，是函数而不是字段。把两类混在一起，是继极对数写错之后"
"最常见的静默集成错误，因为把死区抄到另一座桥上，行为与一台电阻不对的电机"
"完全相同。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:194 ecb868741cea42529fbfe730f4e19377
msgid ""
"The refusal policy completes it: a value that is merely unhelpful is "
"accepted, and a value that is **inconsistent** is refused. An injection "
"amplitude of zero is not \"off\"; it is a request for an observer that "
"cannot work."
msgstr ""
"拒绝策略补全这一层：只是没什么用的取值会被接受，而 **自相矛盾** 的取值会"
"被拒绝。注入幅值取零不是“关掉”，而是在要求一个无法工作的观测器。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:199 c4e214ac51df447fba2f66d9633dbd03
msgid "The memory and concurrency models"
msgstr ""
"内存模型与并发模型"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:201 6b7d6458b21049f2a246974042af1fd7
msgid ""
"There is no allocation anywhere. Fixed-capacity rings, fixed-size "
"observer state, configuration by value. Tracing is switched by changing a"
" **type**, not a flag: the disabled channel is an empty type whose "
"methods the optimiser deletes, so \"off costs nothing\" is structural and"
" the size of the motor does not change with tracing enabled."
msgstr ""
"任何地方都不分配。固定容量的环形缓冲、固定大小的观测器状态、按值传递的配"
"置。轨迹靠换一个 **类型** 来开关，而不是换一个标志位：关闭的通道是一个空"
"类型，其方法被优化器删掉，因此“关掉不花钱”是结构性的，打开轨迹也不改变电"
"机对象的大小。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:206 64dbf7ca354a40d3ad72ff5b1bf8c401
msgid ""
"There is one loop, one context and no locks. Every entry point is written"
" for exactly one caller, and the library does not pretend to be thread-"
"safe by adding mutexes a real-time path cannot afford to take. What it "
"does instead is make the dangerous boundary explicit: the HAL is called "
"from inside the period, so an implementation that blocks has broken the "
"loop's premise -- the contract says so, and the porting checklist asks "
"about it."
msgstr ""
"只有一个环、一个上下文，没有锁。每个入口点都是为唯一一个调用方写的，库也"
"不靠加互斥量来假装线程安全——实时路径付不起取锁的代价。它做的是把危险的边"
"界显式摆出来：HAL 是在周期内部被调用的，所以一个会阻塞的实现已经破坏了环"
"的前提——契约这么写着，移植检查清单也会问到这一点。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:213 81db7c0d72f34e22b200d633d999da4e
msgid "The extension model"
msgstr ""
"扩展模型"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:215 10d0df707e3b40debada8790b9db063f
msgid ""
"There are four seams, and they are one kind of seam: a template parameter"
" whose required interface is a handful of member functions, checked at "
"compile time."
msgstr ""
"接缝有四条，且是同一种接缝：一个模板实参，它要求的接口是若干成员函数，在"
"编译期检查。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:223 f796fd13fd2647b5865b8759fb288d65
msgid ""
"You write one of the boxes on the left; the library names what it needs "
"and checks it when the composition is instantiated."
msgstr ""
"左边方框中的一个由你实现；库声明自己需要什么，并在组合被实例化时检查。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:226 6a8f679c814f4cf7a983d5cde62400c1
msgid ""
"Adding a capability is a compile-time act with three consequences. The "
"cost of the new code is visible in the call graph, because it is inlined "
"where it is used rather than dispatched. A configuration is a type, so "
"two variants are two binaries rather than one binary with a flag -- cheap"
" to reason about, expensive in code size for a large variant matrix. And "
"a wrong implementation fails to compile rather than failing at run time."
msgstr ""
"增加一项能力是编译期的动作，带三个后果。新代码的代价在调用图上看得见，因"
"为它在使用处内联，不是分派过去的。配置是一个类型，所以两个变体是两份二进"
"制，而不是一份二进制加一个标志位——推理便宜，变体矩阵一大就在代码体积上昂"
"贵。写错的实现是编译不过，而不是在运行期失败。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:232 36265e367a74408583f5e0db3c6a77ef
msgid ""
"The seams are deliberately few. A fifth would be a commitment to a fifth "
"kind of variation, and this project would rather add one after seeing the"
" variation twice."
msgstr ""
"接缝是刻意做少的。第五条接缝等于承诺第五种变化，本项目宁愿把一种变化见过"
"两次之后再动手加。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:236 9ec99b41006a4c5681c92b733c180d1d
msgid "The compatibility model"
msgstr ""
"兼容模型"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:238 4f961f29b4dc49079cf09e1b5d0b2c9c
msgid ""
"The C surface is frozen in the way that matters: existing declarations do"
" not change meaning, structures carry their own size so appending a field"
" is compatible, and handles carry a generation counter so a stale one is "
"detected rather than dereferenced. The C++ surface is not frozen the same"
" way, and the asymmetry is deliberate: templates are recompiled, binaries"
" are not."
msgstr ""
"C 使用面在要紧的意义上是冻结的：已有声明不改含义，结构体自带长度，所以追"
"加字段是兼容的；句柄带代数计数器，所以过期的句柄会被检出而不是被解引用。"
"C++ 使用面不以同样的方式冻结，这种不对称是刻意的：模板会被重新编译，二进"
"制不会。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:244 6afe4767319d4e52ae9fff40e0a8b615
msgid ""
"The practical rule is: depend on the C surface when the dependency must "
"survive a rebuild you do not control, and on the templates when you want "
"the inlining."
msgstr ""
"实用规则是：这份依赖必须活过一次不由你掌控的重新构建，就依赖 C 使用面；"
"你要的是内联，就依赖模板。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:248 4f5776667a364d97b23c9ab5c0f7d894
msgid "Where the numbers live"
msgstr ""
"数字各有其家"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:250 2e261324975043e1b9fe23f6c46a73c5
msgid "A fact has one home, and the artefacts that repeat it are generated."
msgstr ""
"一个事实只有一个家，重复它的产物都是生成的。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:257 cbff9a18d7bd4f6186dce73f0844864e
msgid ""
"The registries, the artefacts generated from them, and the gates that "
"would notice a disagreement. The claim table is a registry like the "
"others: its evidence column makes a claim checkable and its basis column "
"makes a change's blast radius computable."
msgstr ""
"注册表、由注册表生成的产物，以及会发现不一致的门禁。主张表和其他注册表同"
"类：它的证据列让一条主张可被检验，它的依据列让一次改动的波及范围可被算出"
"来。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:261 bcbd212ce68f4c24bc4333cbc658c5fe
msgid ""
"This is architecture rather than bookkeeping because it decides what a "
"reviewer can ask. \"Where does this number come from\" has a file answer;"
" \"what would invalidate this claim\" has a file answer; \"what prevents "
"this from rotting\" has a gate answer."
msgstr ""
"这属于架构而不是记账，因为它决定了评审者能问什么。“这个数字从哪来”有一个"
"文件的答案；“什么会让这条主张失效”有一个文件的答案；“什么拦着它腐坏”有一"
"个门禁的答案。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:266 4aeb926e96b14a52a4d3f7eb58b2bb2c
msgid "The costs, and who pays them"
msgstr ""
"代价，以及由谁承担"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:268 dcd1fe4175d44a13a4a3de950aa23067
msgid "Four decisions and their price"
msgstr ""
"四项决定及其价格"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:272 d66821acade1402fb1dd6e7db2783899
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""
"决定"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:273 c66e323fe43749378e5fb56df0731b9d
msgid "Alternative rejected"
msgstr ""
"被否掉的替代方案"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:274 14097b3eb3de427b9df0fb2a55ef1b9c
msgid "What it would have bought"
msgstr ""
"它本可换来什么"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:275 6481054b281a45e8a377bf9db14f9705
msgid "What it costs, and who pays"
msgstr ""
"代价是什么，由谁承担"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:276 8ba3ae64495340f1a34d8c91d6850448
msgid "Composition at compile time"
msgstr ""
"编译期组合"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:277 06f2b574443d41f1bd125825608bcf56
msgid "a run-time interface per component"
msgstr ""
"每个组件一个运行期接口"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:278 59720bb7396a40acb720f9a8c1b2d495
msgid "deciding a variant at run time, one binary for many products"
msgstr ""
"运行期决定变体，一份二进制服务多个产品"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:279 6c4222ccaddc4ac4abe30a38704a3a43
msgid "a factory one level up in the product; the integrator pays"
msgstr ""
"产品里往上挪一层的工厂；由集成者承担"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:280 15374a2dba20482489a46ed7ab379f36
msgid "No exceptions"
msgstr ""
"不用异常"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:281 c3fa2e7e44864813bca5e2172cb6030e
msgid "throwing from deep inside a nested call"
msgstr ""
"从嵌套调用的深处抛出"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:282 d35abfc13c144e90b08375c4815a5372
msgid "error paths that do not lengthen signatures"
msgstr ""
"不拉长签名的错误路径"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:283 0148597cedca40ce944fde74b9aba61d
msgid "every call that can fail returns a value; the author pays"
msgstr ""
"每个可能失败的调用都返回值；由作者承担"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:284 f949ef7de7de472da3f3cce8b0687693
msgid "No allocation"
msgstr ""
"不分配"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:285 01e891ec24f340f7b4e4319185ac0180
msgid "strings, containers, logging in place"
msgstr ""
"就地使用字符串、容器、日志"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:286 4f29ca803ff543329be6cd8cb3029aee
msgid "convenience, and error messages built at the failure site"
msgstr ""
"便利，以及在故障点就地构造的错误信息"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:287 25cf7eb9d9434af197483be4d2ce5e6f
msgid "fault reporting is a code plus a counter; commissioning pays"
msgstr ""
"故障上报是一个码加一个计数器；由投运调试承担"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:288 d2b1fa7e229c4503b7842498f46c4fdd
msgid "Refusals instead of defaults"
msgstr ""
"拒绝，而不是默认值"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:289 a19ec81fe36a4804be704a99ec8b4d07
msgid "a permissive configuration with sensible zeros"
msgstr ""
"一份宽松的、零值看着合理的配置"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:290 1455c3c0543a4c6eaa685bdd3485359a
msgid "a boot that never argues"
msgstr ""
"一次从不争辩的上电"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:291 37f53d832e184cb5a9c518e0b621e8e5
msgid "bring-up friction at least once per board; the integrator pays"
msgstr ""
"每块板至少一次的上板调试摩擦；由集成者承担"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:292 beb415ea47d84f1bb00b56b232737c27
msgid "Frozen C surface"
msgstr ""
"冻结的 C 使用面"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:293 69e255b4e96f43a8bc3f45276dced304
msgid "evolve the C API freely with the templates"
msgstr ""
"让 C API 随模板自由演进"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:294 b3a32319eca948bf8b0eefd5549d85d5
msgid "fewer, simpler declarations"
msgstr ""
"更少、更简单的声明"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:295 7c5a04df83874a329a38b3abf3a1840e
msgid ""
"a size field in every struct crossing the boundary; the binding author "
"pays"
msgstr ""
"每个跨边界的结构体都带一个长度字段；由绑定作者承担"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:297 e8278c18e1274325bd74d49ada7847f6
msgid ""
"None of these is a defect to be fixed later. Each is the other side of a "
"stated constraint, and adopting the library is deciding whether those "
"costs are cheaper than the alternative's."
msgstr ""
"这些都不是留待日后修的缺陷。每一条都是某条已声明约束的另一面；采用这个库"
"，就是在判断这些代价是否比替代方案的代价更便宜。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:301 d59cd8c74ab741adba1ba76f64234082
msgid "How the shape was arrived at"
msgstr ""
"这个形状是怎么来的"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:303 89937a07c5b548ae8045dd28e519cfaf
msgid ""
"History. This section is a record rather than a specification, and the "
"word above is what the documentation's voice gate looks for before it "
"lets a paragraph talk about the past."
msgstr ""
"历史。本节是记录而不是规范，上面那个词就是文档的语气门禁在放行一段谈过去"
"的文字之前要找的东西。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:306 4ac4aa3cc16c42668988ed093b7cc8b0
msgid ""
"The shape converged rather than being designed in one sitting, and the "
"sequence is visible in the repository."
msgstr ""
"这个形状是收敛出来的，不是一次坐下来设计出来的，先后顺序在仓库里看得见。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:309 0e0ae78ad79b4b53b6d625d9c5ecdbcc
msgid ""
"**Refusals came first, and they came from failures.** Each of the four "
"prohibitions began as a defect in something built on top: a loop whose "
"period occasionally overran, an observer that silently did nothing, a "
"configuration that was accepted and produced a drive that merely looked "
"configured. The rule that followed is mechanical -- when a failure is "
"found, the fix is written as a refusal that fails loudly, because a "
"default that keeps working a little is how the same defect returns twice."
msgstr ""
"**拒绝在先，而拒绝来自失败。** 四条禁令中的每一条，起初都是建在其上的某"
"个东西里的一个缺陷：一个周期偶尔超期的环、一个悄悄什么都不做的观测器、一"
"份被接受却只造出一台看着像配置好了的驱动器的配置。随之定下的规则是机械的"
"——发现一次失败，就把修法写成一条会大声失败的拒绝，因为一个“还能凑合工作"
"一点”的默认值，正是同一个缺陷回来两次的方式。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:316 407ff534f6aa4740a6ee49bf21229ab0
msgid ""
"**The registries came from documentation drift.** Documentation that "
"carried numbers in prose stopped being true. The response was not to "
"check harder but to give each fact a file and generate everything that "
"repeats it, then add a gate that compares the documented copy with the "
"artefact -- which is why the site and the manual both draw their numbers "
"from registries."
msgstr ""
"**注册表来自文档漂移。** 把数字写在散文里的文档，不再为真。应对的办法不"
"是检查得更勤，而是给每个事实一个文件，把一切重复它的东西生成出来，再加一"
"道门禁，把文档里的副本与产物做比较——站点和手册的数字都取自注册表，原因就"
"在这里。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:321 e43b88e190764d5aa4da7ec01f7a4071
msgid ""
"**The evidence model came from a claim nothing could contradict.** A "
"statement was found that had passed every check because no check was "
"about it. The claim table, the case pointer in both directions, and the "
"basis graph all date from that discovery, and the correction is recorded "
"publicly in :doc:`foundation-log`."
msgstr ""
"**证据模型来自一条没有任何东西能反驳的主张。** 当时发现有一句话通过了所"
"有检查，因为没有任何一项检查是针对它的。主张表、双向的用例指针、依据图，"
"都始于那一次发现，纠正过程公开记录在 :doc:`foundation-log` 里。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:326 3431723bed58476b89c15f6af3bda728
msgid ""
"**The C face came from a versioning problem, not from a portability "
"wish.** The binary boundary exists because consumers were recompiling the"
" templates and the semantics were drifting between them. Freezing the C "
"surface forced the semantics into declarations, and the other bindings "
"then had something stable to bind to."
msgstr ""
"**C 使用面来自一个版本问题，而不是可移植性的愿望。** 二进制边界之所以存"
"在，是因为使用方各自重新编译模板，语义在它们之间漂移。冻结 C 使用面把语"
"义逼进了声明里，其他绑定于是有了稳定的东西可绑。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:331 6ad03bd49d9742b1a43d1070afe28e8a
msgid ""
"**The infrastructure layer is byte-pinned on purpose.** The build system "
"and the formatting and linting configuration are not edited by hand; they"
" are owned outside this library and checked byte for byte, because a "
"project that lets its own build files drift cannot make claims about "
"anybody else's builds."
msgstr ""
"**基础设施层是刻意按字节钉住的。** 构建系统与格式、lint 配置都不手工编辑"
"；它们归本库之外所有，并逐字节比对，因为一个任由自己的构建文件漂移的项目"
"，无法对他人的构建作出任何主张。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:336 707f2942cbfb4d6598a416ce4e140d23
msgid ""
"The practical lesson is the one worth carrying: each decision above is a "
"response to something that had already gone wrong, each is cheap to "
"describe and expensive to retrofit, and the shape is what survived."
msgstr ""
"值得带走的是那条实用教训：上面每一项决定都是对某件已经出错之事的回应，每"
"一条描述起来便宜、事后补装昂贵，留下来的就是现在的形状。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:341 339846bf259549e59dc05eecfcbb63ed
msgid "How to review the architecture"
msgstr ""
"如何评审这套架构"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:343 4632098fa6fc454dbcd7c0a7aaf6bfed
msgid ""
"Does the periodic path allocate, throw, or dispatch virtually? The build "
"disables two of the three; the third is checked by reading the "
"composition, which is a type."
msgstr ""
"周期路径会分配、会抛异常、会做虚分派吗？三者之中构建禁掉了两个；第三个靠"
"读组合来检查，而组合是一个类型。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:345 c443f74d3ad147229fc4d953d2faaa24
msgid ""
"Can a consumer reach the core without going through a declared face? The "
"layering picture is the claim; the include face is the check."
msgstr ""
"使用方能否不经过某个已声明的使用面就够到内核？分层图是主张，include 面是"
"检查。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:347 e667d76607914e809b7e71e4d59a04ec
msgid ""
"Is every fact in one place, and is disagreement detectable? The "
"registries and the gates answer it, and the answer is checkable by "
"running them."
msgstr ""
"每个事实是否只有一处出处，不一致是否可被发现？注册表和门禁回答这个问题；"
"回答能否成立，把它们跑一遍就知道。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:349 0136714af1f84d0ab72934d7b1b92f73
msgid ""
"What happens when a configuration is wrong? It is refused, with a code "
"that separates \"you asked wrong\" from \"this build cannot\"."
msgstr ""
"配置写错时会发生什么？会被拒绝，并给出一个把“你问错了”和“这次构建做不到”"
"分开的错误码。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:351 cbe8988fc76041f3a033ae1f594b3704
msgid ""
"How does a new capability enter? Through one of four seams, at compile "
"time, with its interface checked by the compiler and its behaviour "
"checked by a case."
msgstr ""
"一项新能力怎么进来？经由四条接缝之一，在编译期进来；接口由编译器检查，行"
"为由一条用例检查。"

#: ../../source/architecture.rst:353 b80cde69c208496bac4f16708407f548
msgid ""
"What does the architecture refuse to do, and is that written down? This "
"page and :doc:`boundaries`, in that order."
msgstr ""
"这套架构拒绝做什么，这写下来了吗？本页与 :doc:`boundaries` ，就是这个顺"
"序。"

